(text "neo-mem-compact: 2048K memory board v2 (CoCo 3 2 MB SRAM, plugs into CN4/CN5/CN6)" (at 25.40 30.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 772cd154-4302-4aa0-adda-e8440efc5260))
(text "Remove IC16-IC19 and cut C65, C66 first (as for any 512K upgrade)." (at 25.40 35.56 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 458af0b2-73a8-4253-a9bb-2a3770eaae7a))
(text "J3 (2x2, bank row + ground row, same layout as the GIME-Z and DAT J2) takes BANK0/BANK1 (physical A19/A20). Unconnected: R1/R2 pull low = 512K mode." (at 25.40 40.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 3cddf7b3-ca70-4aeb-a7c2-eefb46702f28))
(text "Write logic (active low): ~BHE = ~WE0 XOR 1   ~BLE = ~WE1 XOR 1   ~WE = ~WE1 XOR ~BHE" (at 160.02 30.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 229ef742-a7af-49ce-8c34-679dd6918702))
(text "RAS = ~RAS XOR 1 clocks U3/U4: row address (9 bits) and BANK1:0 latched on the falling edge of ~RAS." (at 160.02 35.56 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 8b34522f-60e5-4cb0-ac8f-3af8e800a73f))
(text "SRAM ~CE1 = ~CAS, CE2 = BYTE = 1 (x16), ~OE = 0. Address/data pin order is permuted for routing." (at 160.02 40.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 75485b13-5d37-4dae-975b-fe4f116963c7))
(text "Derived from cc3-512k by Ciaran Anscomb (CC BY-SA 4.0), logic per Jim Brain. This design is CC BY-SA 4.0." (at 25.40 256.54 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 2c047580-b0ec-4374-b12e-3c24ec8dcebf))
